{"id":"m2://rec/open_logic/content/model-theory/interpolation/interpolation-proof.tex#thm:interpol#1","source":"open_logic","snapshot":"blake3:a5eb116529d3e799289dd9f7e7530d0d446b3615f5608fe08c668241eee3c765","locator":"https://github.com/OpenLogicProject/OpenLogic/blob/1e960beff9ed7835bf3e3f1335e21af3439cd107/content/model-theory/interpolation/interpolation-proof.tex#L13","native_id":"content/model-theory/interpolation/interpolation-proof.tex#thm:interpol","kind":"statement","name":"Craig's Interpolation Theorem","text":"If $\\Entails !A \\lif !B$, then there is !!a{sentence} $!C$ such that\n$\\Entails !A \\lif !C$ and $\\Entails !C \\lif !B$, and every\n!!{constant}, !!{function}, and !!{predicate} (other than $\\eq$) in\n$!C$ occurs both in $!A$ and~$!B$. The !!{sentence} $!C$ is called an\n\\emph{interpolant} of $!A$ and~$!B$.","class":"open","by":"textbook/1","resource":"PKGMM3P5QY","at":{"section":"46.10","kind":"thm"}}
